  "controlled_comparison_has_a_near_fixed_sign": "The controlled arms are DETERMINISTIC argmax-utility policies, which are monotone non-decreasing in utility, so an immediate two-cycle requires an exact utility tie and is close to structurally excluded. 'Control has less cycling than a stochastic sampler' is therefore largely definitional and is NOT clean evidence that control suppresses cycling. It is reported as context. The falsifiable comparison is r_theta versus empirical_family: both are stochastic samplers over the identical support, so a difference between them could have come out either way.",
